34,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"It seems like the treasurer has to spend a lot of time chasing money every month. That sounds really tiring for them. Also, the same people are always doing the setup and locking up.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The fixed costs for hall hire and insurance are quite high, making up seventy percent of our outgoings. Additionally, many members struggle to pay their renewals on time or in one lump sum.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,"It seems we are losing potential members. Many who attend taster evenings are hesitant to commit to a full year upfront, and mid-year joiners require tedious manual calculations for their fees.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"It's a bit worrying, actually. Turnout for our weekday evenings has dropped significantly since the summer, and some of our quieter members feel uneasy about the cost per visit. It's like they're second-guessing coming out.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It's a classic case of the ""dedicated few"" carrying the entire club. A quarter of us are doing two-thirds of the attending, and the same nine people are handling all the grunt work. It's hardly a fair distribution.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, if people struggle with lump sums, maybe that's why the treasurer has to spend so many hours chasing money? It seems like a lot of work for one person.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"That is a logical connection. If a significant number of members cannot pay upfront, the administrative burden of chasing payments and managing installments naturally increases.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@May, if members are second-guessing their attendance due to the cost per visit, it suggests our current structure might be creating a psychological barrier for those who aren't as committed.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly! It's like they're calculating the ""value"" of a night out instead of just coming to see their friends. That kind of hesitation is a total mood-killer for the club's energy.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, the treasurer's exhaustion isn't just about chasing money; it's about the resentment that builds when the same nine people are the only ones showing up to lock the doors. We're running a club, not a private party for the elite.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I didn't think about the resentment part, but that sounds sad. I just hope we can find a way to make it easier for everyone, so nobody feels too tired or unhappy.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"We must prioritize a structure that ensures our fixed costs are covered without relying on guesswork. If seventy percent of our spending is non-negotiable, we cannot afford a system that makes payment unpredictable.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"We need to balance financial stability with accessibility. If we make the entry barrier too high or the payment process too rigid, we risk alienating newcomers and those who only attend occasionally.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, I get the need for stability, but if we're too rigid, we'll just have a perfectly funded club with nobody in it! We need to make it feel effortless to show up.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, ""effortless"" is a luxury for those who don't have to lock up the hall. If we make it too easy for the ghosts to drift in and out, we're just subsidizing their leisure with the labor of the regulars.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I hope we can find a way to help the treasurer too. If chasing money takes six hours a month, that's a lot of time they can't spend enjoying the club with us.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"Regardless of the treasurer's time, the financial reality is that we have high fixed costs. We need a system that guarantees these are met while acknowledging that some members cannot pay in one lump sum.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,"It seems we are facing a conflict between administrative ease, financial security, and member inclusivity. We must find a solution that doesn't discourage newcomers or burden the treasurer with manual calculations.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"I just want us to get back that feeling where people just show up because they want to be here. If we overthink the fees, we're just killing the vibe. Let's keep it simple!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Simple is great for those who don't do the work, May. But ""simple"" usually means the regulars pay for the ghosts and do the cleaning. We need a structure that actually reflects who is using the club.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
